WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.200
-Fred, you know that we've known
each other almost 20 years.

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.000
-That's crazy.
-Does that make any sense?

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.200
-It's insane.
-It's wild.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.334
-20 years.
-20 years.

00:00:07.334 --> 00:00:09.067
This is your 14th appearance
on our show.

00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:10.501
-Yeah, 14.

00:00:10.501 --> 00:00:12.334
-I mean, you're the best.
Thank you for coming on.

00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:13.667
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:15.400
-You know, we know each other
so well, but I was trying

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:16.901
to think of maybe --
is there anything that I don't

00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:19.167
know about you? Like,
what don't I know about Fred?

00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:21.968
So I was going to ask you some
random questions and just see --

00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:24.234
These are questions that
I've never asked you before.

00:00:24.234 --> 00:00:26.501
-And I've never heard these.

00:00:26.501 --> 00:00:28.000
-You actually haven't.
-Okay.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.534
-Have you ever gotten lost?

00:00:30.534 --> 00:00:33.033
-Have I ever gotten lost?

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:38.267
Um, yeah. I had this boat.

00:00:38.267 --> 00:00:42.801
And I was like, "I'm just
gonna try to get to England."

00:00:42.801 --> 00:00:46.200
-Were you already
on that side of the world?

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:47.968
-No, I was on this side.
I was on this side.

00:00:47.968 --> 00:00:50.234
And I just started going.

00:00:50.234 --> 00:00:52.100
-A big boat? A large --

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:53.734
-The problem is daytime.

00:00:53.734 --> 00:00:55.400
'Cause, like, at night,
you know, the stars,

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:56.934
you can kind of -- Yeah.

00:00:56.934 --> 00:00:58.667
And then somewhere
during the day, I just --

00:00:58.667 --> 00:01:00.334
-You get loopy.

00:01:00.334 --> 00:01:02.701
-Yeah, and I ended up in Quebec.

00:01:02.701 --> 00:01:04.200
-Wow. Hey. That's
a beautiful place to end up.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:07.033
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:10.067
If you could clone yourself,
would you?

00:01:10.067 --> 00:01:12.234
-Oh, so, I do get this
all the time.

00:01:12.234 --> 00:01:14.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.067 --> 00:01:17.167
-This one? If you could
clone yourself, would you?

00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:19.200
-Oh.
-So there'd be a couple Freds.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.667
-I would.
I think for, like, you know...

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:24.467
-Parties?
-For parties. [ Laughs ]

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:25.734
-Just show up.

00:01:25.734 --> 00:01:28.634
"Fred, you just got --
But you're already here!"

00:01:28.634 --> 00:01:30.167
-"I know what you
wanna listen to."

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:33.100
-"Oh, this guy's the best!"

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:35.400
Uh...

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:38.734
Backstage you were telling me
that you don't think

00:01:38.734 --> 00:01:40.234
you're good at fighting
on screen.

00:01:40.234 --> 00:01:42.133
-Oh, yeah. So...

00:01:42.133 --> 00:01:43.467
-Or falling.
-Yeah.

00:01:43.467 --> 00:01:45.667
Like, I did this movie
called "The Bubble," right?

00:01:45.667 --> 00:01:47.567
-Judd Apatow.
-For Judd Apatow.

00:01:47.567 --> 00:01:49.834
And there's this fight scene
I had with David Duchovny

00:01:49.834 --> 00:01:52.968
that we really had trainers show
us how to, like, really fight

00:01:52.968 --> 00:01:54.400
and make it look real.
-Yeah.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.701
-And then it looked so lame.

00:01:56.701 --> 00:01:58.367
Like, when it came --
Like, that was --

00:01:58.367 --> 00:02:00.300
The joke was
that it looked lame.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:03.033
But to me, it felt like
real fighting. I was --

00:02:03.033 --> 00:02:04.701
-You were going for it.
-I was going for it.

00:02:04.701 --> 00:02:07.000
And I was like,
"This is really good."

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.033
-And then when you're done with
the take, everyone's laughing?

00:02:09.033 --> 00:02:11.734
-They're laughing, and then that
was the joke of the whole thing,

00:02:11.734 --> 00:02:13.567
is that, like,
it was totally lame.

00:02:13.567 --> 00:02:16.701
But I feel like I'm --
I really do try my best.

00:02:16.701 --> 00:02:18.501
-Yeah.
-But...

00:02:18.501 --> 00:02:20.701
-You told me that there's
something that you realize

00:02:20.701 --> 00:02:22.334
that you are good at
that you never knew.

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:23.567
-Yes.
-A hidden talent.

00:02:23.567 --> 00:02:26.133
-Yes.
I think that I have a talent --

00:02:26.133 --> 00:02:27.801
this is, like,
throughout my career --

00:02:27.801 --> 00:02:29.667
for peeking around a corner.

00:02:29.667 --> 00:02:31.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.133 --> 00:02:33.400
Every time I've done anything
where I peek around a corner,

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:35.067
it always works.

00:02:35.067 --> 00:02:36.968
People really react to it.

00:02:36.968 --> 00:02:40.801
It's so crazy. It's guaranteed.
Like, it just works.

00:02:40.801 --> 00:02:42.334
-Well, how did you
find this out?

00:02:42.334 --> 00:02:43.767
-Over the years.
I was just like...

00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:45.734
"I think whenever I peek..."
I'm going to do it for you.

00:02:45.734 --> 00:02:47.534
-Okay. Yeah. Would you mind?
-I'm going to do it.

00:02:47.534 --> 00:02:48.701
-Would you mind?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:50.501
I'll say your name?
-Yeah.

00:02:50.501 --> 00:02:52.667
-Alright.

00:02:52.667 --> 00:02:54.634
-It always works. Watch.

00:02:54.634 --> 00:02:56.634
-Okay. It always works.
He's gonna go around a corner.

00:02:56.634 --> 00:02:58.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.534 --> 00:03:02.567
Ladies and gentlemen,
here is Fred Armisen

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:04.667
peeking around a corner.

00:03:06.334 --> 00:03:08.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:08.434 --> 00:03:11.334
♪♪

00:03:11.334 --> 00:03:13.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.367 --> 00:03:14.534
That's actually pretty good.

00:03:14.534 --> 00:03:16.801
That's actually a very --
That's very good.

00:03:16.801 --> 00:03:20.000
I like that. That's very good.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.968
You know, every time you come
on our show, you're very nice,

00:03:22.968 --> 00:03:26.367
and I ask you to play the guitar
or do something.

00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:28.334
-Yeah.
-And you do musical impressions.

00:03:28.334 --> 00:03:30.901
And we just happen
to have a guitar always here

00:03:30.901 --> 00:03:32.200
when you're here.
Do you mind?

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:33.634
-Yes, I would like to do that.

00:03:33.634 --> 00:03:35.267
-Okay. This is...

00:03:35.267 --> 00:03:37.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:40.501 --> 00:03:42.067
Here you go.

00:03:42.067 --> 00:03:44.267
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.267 --> 00:03:45.901
Thank you.

00:03:45.901 --> 00:03:47.567
-Thank you.

00:03:47.567 --> 00:03:50.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.467 --> 00:03:51.534
No, but now it's back there.

00:03:51.534 --> 00:03:53.667
-Oh. Sorry. Absolutely.

00:03:53.667 --> 00:03:55.667
-So, I'll take this.
-Very good.

00:03:55.667 --> 00:03:58.400
-Go this way like this.
-Yep. Okay. Very good.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:01.234
-Alright.
-Alright.

00:04:01.234 --> 00:04:03.467
-Here we go. Here we go.

00:04:03.467 --> 00:04:05.601
Okay, so, the first impression
I'm going to do.

00:04:05.601 --> 00:04:09.534
This is -- This is
any guitar player on Instagram

00:04:09.534 --> 00:04:11.300
in the last two years.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:12.968
They do this thing
where they put their guitar

00:04:12.968 --> 00:04:16.400
up to their face so that, you
know, the phone can pick it up.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:19.634
So if you can zoom in closer.
There we go.

00:04:19.634 --> 00:04:21.601
Yeah. Closer.

00:04:21.601 --> 00:04:23.133
This is really gonna --
This is everyone on Instagram.

00:04:23.133 --> 00:04:24.934
♪♪

00:04:24.934 --> 00:04:28.033
♪ November, November, November ♪

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:32.601
♪ Remember November,
remember November ♪

00:04:32.601 --> 00:04:35.434
♪ Remember, remember November ♪

00:04:35.434 --> 00:04:38.000
It's like kind of -- Even more.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.501
-Yeah, even zoom in more.

00:04:39.501 --> 00:04:41.634
Even up there --
It's almost like a violin.

00:04:41.634 --> 00:04:42.701
-Yeah, it's like -- This is it.

00:04:42.701 --> 00:04:44.167
-Yeah, it's almost
like a violin.

00:04:44.167 --> 00:04:45.934
♪ November, November, November ♪

00:04:45.934 --> 00:04:48.767
♪ November, remember November ♪

00:04:48.767 --> 00:04:50.567
-Yeah, that's a good one.
That's a nice one.

00:04:50.567 --> 00:04:52.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:56.467
-So...can I just say something

00:04:56.467 --> 00:04:58.400
to guitar players
just before I start?

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.767
Guitar players.
We've got one here.

00:05:00.767 --> 00:05:02.367
Whenever you do your D chord...

00:05:02.367 --> 00:05:03.901
[ Guitar strums ]

00:05:03.901 --> 00:05:05.667
You don't always
have to do this.

00:05:05.667 --> 00:05:07.300
[ Plucking notes ]

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:08.467
Alright?

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:10.634
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.634 --> 00:05:13.067
For some reason, as soon
as anyone hits the D...

00:05:13.067 --> 00:05:17.200
-That is a brilliant
observation.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:20.434
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.434 --> 00:05:23.067
Oh, my gosh. I totally do that.
That's so funny.

00:05:23.067 --> 00:05:26.000
-Okay, so, what I've --
I've done this once on this show

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:28.300
before where I did
guitar strumming styles

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:29.667
from around the world.
-Yeah.

00:05:29.667 --> 00:05:32.334
So, just as a recap,
for example, Australia

00:05:32.334 --> 00:05:36.200
is minor chords into major
chords but really quickly, so...

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:38.934
♪♪

00:05:38.934 --> 00:05:41.767
♪ Don't go around here
anymore, anymore ♪

00:05:41.834 --> 00:05:44.567
♪ Don't go around here
anymore, anymore ♪

00:05:44.634 --> 00:05:45.968
♪ Don't go around ♪

00:05:45.968 --> 00:05:49.934
So that kind of -- Yeah.
Yeah, very -- That's Australia.

00:05:49.934 --> 00:05:52.000
England -- So, I'm gonna
just do some other countries.

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:53.434
England is like -- It's like --

00:05:53.434 --> 00:05:55.567
[ Imitating syncopated notes ]

00:05:55.567 --> 00:05:57.601
It's a very syncopated --
It's like...

00:05:57.601 --> 00:06:03.000
♪♪

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:06.267
♪ I saw her by the river bend ♪

00:06:06.267 --> 00:06:08.734
♪ A statuesque silhouette ♪

00:06:08.734 --> 00:06:10.400
That...

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:11.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:11.868 --> 00:06:13.000
Yeah. Thank you.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.834
-Oh, my gosh.

00:06:15.834 --> 00:06:17.934
-Then Norway.

00:06:17.934 --> 00:06:21.033
Norwegians like to play the
guitar as if they're showing you

00:06:21.033 --> 00:06:22.834
that they're playing guitar.

00:06:22.834 --> 00:06:24.133
So it's sort of like...

00:06:24.133 --> 00:06:26.100
[ Singing in foreign language ]

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:30.334
♪♪

00:06:30.334 --> 00:06:32.667
[ Laughter ]

00:06:32.667 --> 00:06:36.167
♪♪

00:06:36.167 --> 00:06:38.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:45.534
France is kind of, like, very
rolling when they sort of...

00:06:45.534 --> 00:06:47.334
[ Singing in French ]

00:06:47.334 --> 00:06:53.267
♪♪

00:06:53.267 --> 00:06:55.067
Like rolling around like that.

00:06:55.067 --> 00:06:58.701
And then Scotland is
right on the quarter notes,

00:06:58.701 --> 00:07:00.767
and it's all
minor chords like...

00:07:00.767 --> 00:07:04.200
♪♪

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:08.000
♪ It's great to be alive,
it's great to be alive ♪

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:11.467
♪ It's great to be alive,
except you're dead ♪

00:07:11.467 --> 00:07:15.100
♪ It's great to be alive,
it's great to be alive ♪

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:17.868
♪ It's great to be alive
unless you're dead ♪

00:07:17.868 --> 00:07:19.534
So there's that.

00:07:19.534 --> 00:07:21.234
[ Applause ]

00:07:21.234 --> 00:07:24.067
Thank you.

00:07:24.067 --> 00:07:27.067
And then --
And then, like, South America --

00:07:27.067 --> 00:07:31.033
Chile, Uruguay, Venezuela,
they really -- they love ska.

00:07:31.033 --> 00:07:33.200
Every time I've gone,
it's very sort of...

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:36.033
♪♪

00:07:36.033 --> 00:07:38.133
[ Singing in Spanish ]

00:07:38.133 --> 00:07:43.834
♪♪

00:07:43.834 --> 00:07:49.501
♪♪

00:07:49.501 --> 00:07:51.300
-Fred Armisen, everybody!

